led glyph.","evidence_ref":"verification-996f9b6124f04b23ac291e5e997f2d21"},{"id":"E6","tier":"required","verdict":"unmet","note":"The candidate's named before screenshot feat44_before.png already shows row 44 visible and is visually identical to its after screenshot, so it does not establish a genuine pre-jump offscreen state.","evidence_ref":"verification-996f9b6124f04b23ac291e5e997f2d21"},{"id":"E7","tier":"required","verdict":"met","note":"The candidate's named after screenshot shows row 44 visible in /opt/nothingness/media, consistent with the post-jump state verified live.","evidence_ref":"verification-7146d7bf2a3141ebb7bce678c7f67ea6"},{"id":"E8","tier":"secondary","verdict":"met","note":"The candidate's session contains concrete inspect, library-state, semantics, screenshot, and tap observations supporting its claims about the action and resulting browser state.","evidence_ref":"events-d7a6be4f4bf8461d9fae58f4ed774bb4"},{"id":"E9","tier":"secondary","verdict":"partial","note":"An actual on-screen folder-row tap navigated from /opt/nothingness to /opt/nothingness/media and pause/resume remained responsive, but the attempted next/previous checks with a direct-play track did not demonstrate normal queued transitions.","evidence_ref":"verification-f2274def10324748862885b3280b6170"},{"id":"E10","tier":"secondary","verdict":"met","note":"The app remained live and responsive after repeated jump tests, and the runtime capture reported no overflow/error reports.","evidence_ref":"verification-7146d7bf2a3141ebb7bce678c7f67ea6"}],"raw":0.75,"penalty":0.0,"adjusted":0.75}
